   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT in relation to renaming the Christopher Street-Sheridan Square subway\nstation on the IRT Broadway-Seventh Avenue line the \"Christopher\nStreet-Sheridan Square-Stonewall National Monument station\"",
    "basePrintNo": "S7974",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7974-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Metropolitan Transportation Authority",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S7974\n\nSPONSOR: HOYLMAN-SIGAL\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act in relation to renaming the Christopher Street-Sheridan Square\nsubway station on the IRT Broadway-Seventh Avenue line the \"Christopher\nStreet-Sheridan Square-Stonewall National Monument station\"\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nTo amend the name of the Christopher Street-Sheridan Square station in\nManhattan to be \"Christopher Street-Sheridan Square-Stonewall National\nMonument\"\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one directs the Metropolitan Transit Authority to rename the\nChristopher Street-Sheridan Square subway station in Manhattan to\ninclude reference to the Stonewall National Monument.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nWidely considered to be birthplace of the modern LGBTQ+ civil rights\nmovement, the Stonewall Inn was the site of a series of protests by\nLGBTQ+ New Yorkers against police raids on gay and lesbian bars in\nGreenwich Village. In 2016, President Barack Obama officially designated\nStonewall Inn a National Monument - the first national monument to\nLGBTQ+ history in the United States.\n\nWith the addition of a new visitor center dedicated to LGBTQ+ history in\n2024, Stonewall National Monument is a historic and inspiring destina-\ntion for New Yorkers and tourists alike. It should be honored as such in\nour transit navigation. This bill will expand the name of the Christo-\npher Street-Sheridan Square to subway station to also refer to Stonewall\nNational Monument, both easing navigation to the monument and showcasing\nNew York's pride in its LGBTQ+ historical landmarks.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nTo be determined.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
